I am at the Infopark office.
It is the morning tea break now.
Prakash and I usually drink tea together at this time.
We are sitting and talking in the cafeteria.
Suddenly, a message comes on my phone.
I take the phone and look.
It is an official message.
It has come from my mobile service provider.
Very formal language is used in it.
"Your details are required to be updated to maintain the connection."
I feel a little afraid when I read that.
Will they cancel my phone connection?
I show the phone's screen to Prakash.
"Prakash, look at this."
"Is there a problem?" I ask.
Prakash reads that message.
And then he smiles.
"This is a standard message, Maya," Prakash says.
"Companies usually send messages like this to customers."
"This is just a standard check."
Hearing that, I feel a great relief.
